  "text": "[warm] Every estate collects something. Mine collects phenomena. [short pause] This is why the sky is blue — not a diagram of it: the actual sieve, running. Short waves scatter out of the beam and fill the dome; long waves barrel through; at sunset the beam grows so long that only red survives it.\n\n[pause] And this is the far end of the same story. Two slits, one particle at a time. Each arrives as a single dot — yet the dots pile up into interference fringes. [short pause] I fired those just now, while you watched. [pause] Light will not tell you what it is. I find that endlessly companionable — an estate full of proofs, anchored by a thing that refuses to be settled.",
